CM_ "V_1.0";
CM_ BO_ 2499759204 "Back up speaker handshake signal from pack 1 to pack 2";
CM_ SG_ 2499759204 BATT_speakerClaimFlag_1 "Default speaker pack will set this bit to 1.
Default speaker pack shall set this signal to 0 in case of BATT_expectedSpeakerID_2 becomes 2.";
CM_ SG_ 2499759204 BATT_expectedSpeakerID_1 "Default Speaker pack shall set this signal to 1.
Default pack shall set this signal to 2 in case of BATT_expectedSpeakerID_2 becomes 2.
";
CM_ SG_ 2499759460 BATT_speakerClaimFlag_2 "Backup speaker pack shall set this signal to 0.
Backup speaker pack shall set this signal to 1 if BATT_speakerClaimFlag_1 set to 0.
";
CM_ SG_ 2499759460 BATT_expectedSpeakerID_2 "Backup speaker pack shall set this signal to 1.
Backup speaker shall set this signal to 2 in case of default speaker disconnect detected.
";
CM_ BO_ 2499756361 "pack ID arbitration trigger command from the VCU";
CM_ BO_ 2499761508 "SOH  signals communicating string resistance information calculated from all strings.";
CM_ BO_ 2499760996 "SOH signals communicating string capacity related information calculated from all strings.";
CM_ BO_ 2499760740 "String Voltage signals communicating string information limted to strings that are connected to High Voltage (contactors closed).";
CM_ BO_ 2499756388 "Temperature signals communicating string information limted to strings that are connected to High Voltage (contactors closed).";
CM_ BO_ 2499757668 "SOC / Energy signals communicating string information limted to strings that are connected to High Voltage (contactors closed).";
CM_ BO_ 2499761764 "Voltage signals communicating string information limted to strings that are connected to High Voltage (contactors closed).";
CM_ BO_ 2499760484 "This message contains the results from the last Isolation Resistance Test.  The system always runs an Isolation Test after contactors open and may run an Isolation Test at start-up.  See integration guide for more information";
CM_ BO_ 2499760228 "Signals related to Charging Limits, are calculated by the Battery Management System.";
CM_ BO_ 2499756105 "This Message is the only message that is required for the XPAND System to operate. See individual signal comments and the Integration Guide.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_MaxStringsToCharge "BMS should compare the value to the number of strings in the system, and the BMS will determine if the value passed by APP_Command:APP_MaxStringsToConnect";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_State_ReqMode "A signal from the Application that requests that the Battery Management System enter Charge/Discharge Mode.
This only works if Contactor_Command is Close & APP_Comm_RollingCount is incrementing.
See Value Descriptions";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Contactor_Command "A signal from the Application that requests that the Battery Management System closes contactors.
This only works if App_StateReqMode is Charge/Discharge & APP_Comm_RollingCount is incrementing.
See Value Descriptions";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Balancing_Enable_F "Signal from the Application that communicates to the Battery Management System that Cell Balance (if neccessary) is allowed.
See Value Descriptions tab for more information.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_Comm_RollingCount "An incrementing signal from the Application that the Battery Management System used to calculate freshness.
The Application should increment (with rollover) this signal every time it's message is transmitted to the Battery Management System.

";
CM_ SG_ 2499756105 APP_IsoRes_Enable_F "CURRENTLY NOT SUPPORTED.  Signal from the Application that communicates to the Battery Management System that Runtime Isolation Detection is allowed.
See Value Descriptions tab for more information.";
CM_ BO_ 2499756132 "These signals communicate the state of the Battery Management System.  Look here for an overal understanding of the state of the BMS.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Comm_StringsAddressed "This signal communicates the number of strings addressed at initialization";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Contactor_EmergencyOpen_F "This signal communicates if there was a Battery Management Fault that necessitated the contactors opening immediately.  If this happens, there will be a Fault flag set in BATT_Diagnostics
";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_HVIL_Status "This signal communicates the high level status of the HVIL.   See the Value Description";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Balancing_Status "This signal communicates if a string in the BMS is currently balancing. See the Value Description";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_State_SysPwrMd "This signal communicates the overal state of the System. When in Partial Run or Run, one or more strings are connected to High Voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Contactor_StringsConnected "This signal communicates the number of strings connected to High Voltage at any given time.";
CM_ SG_ 2499756132 BATT_Comm_RollingCount "An ever incrementing signal that the Application can chose to monitor to ensure the BMS is sending fresh information with each message.";
CM_ BO_ 2499756644 "Signals related to String Current as calculated by the Battery Management System.";
CM_ BO_ 2499756900 "String Voltage signals communicating string information calculated from all strings connected or not connected.";
CM_ BO_ 2499757156 "Cell Voltage signals communicating string information calculated from all strings connected or not connected.";
CM_ BO_ 2499757412 "SOC / Energy signals communicating string information calculated from all strings connected or not connected.";
CM_ BO_ 2499757924 "Temperature signals communicating string information calculated from all strings connected or not connected.";
CM_ BO_ 2499758180 "Signals related to Discharging Limits, are calculated by the Battery Management System.";
CM_ BO_ 2499758436 "Signals related to Regen Limits, are calculated by the Battery Management System.";
